## Affordable is a decision
<!-- claim -->
**{{ v('ch1.message') }}**
<!-- step: price -->
Two numbers claim to measure the same thing. The first is the price of the median home divided by the median household income in the same metro. It is the number most stories lead with, and it moves slowly, because incomes and prices both compound. Across the {{ v('ch1.metros_compared') }} metropolitan areas in both the price index and the census release, weighted by owner households, the ratio stood at {{ v('ch1.first.price_to_income') }} in {{ v('ch1.first_year') }} and {{ v('ch1.latest.price_to_income') }} in {{ v('ch1.latest_year') }}, a change of {{ v('ch1.pti_change') }} over the whole span. The peak of the last cycle was {{ v('ch1.peak.price_to_income') }} in {{ v('ch1.peak_year') }}.
<!-- step: payment -->
The second number is what the same home costs to carry: the monthly payment on a thirty year mortgage with {{ v('policy.down_payment_share') }} down at the rate of each quarter, twelve of them divided by the median income. That is the number a household lives with. It stood at {{ v('ch1.first.payment_share') }} in {{ v('ch1.first_year') }}, fell for a decade as rates fell, and in {{ v('ch1.latest_year') }} it is {{ v('ch1.latest.payment_share') }} (interval {{ v('ch1.latest.payment_share.low') }} to {{ v('ch1.latest.payment_share.high') }}), against a government line of {{ v('policy.affordable_line') }}.
<!-- step: peak -->
Set the two side by side and the story of the last twenty years splits in half. The price story took two decades. The payment story happened between the first rate rise and the eighteen months that followed it. In {{ v('ch1.latest_year') }} the payment share sits {{ v('ch1.diff') }} against the {{ v('ch1.peak_year') }} peak (interval {{ v('ch1.diff.low') }} to {{ v('ch1.diff.high') }}), and {{ v('ch1.metros_above_peak') }} of the {{ v('ch1.metros_compared') }} metros ({{ v('ch1.metros_above_peak_share') }}) now sit above their own {{ v('ch1.peak_year') }} payment share. {{ v('ch1.metros_above_line') }} metros ({{ v('ch1.metros_above_line_share') }}) sit above the {{ v('policy.affordable_line') }} line for the median household. Affordable is a decision about which of these two numbers you let define the word.
